      "bug": "lc-17q",
      "why": "A removal is a fact any author can state and none can retract, so deletedAt is unioned rather than raced and the instant kept is the EARLIEST reported — a later author republishing the tombstone is repeating that removal, not performing a new one. The section leaves the result only once nothing live is left in it on any slice: s-old is tombstoned but still holds someone's live item and stays; s-gone is tombstoned and empty and is dropped, its tombstoned item with it.",
